cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  ProofLayer: Automated Cybersecurity Compliance Auditing for
  State Government Policies via Multi-LLM Orchestration
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite the paper. If you
  need to cite the artefact itself, use the second entry under
  references.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Trivedi
    given-names: Devharsh
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6374-7249'
    affiliation: 'Bowie State University, MD, USA'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/devharsh/Claude-Files/tree/main/prooflayer'
abstract: >-
  Compliance auditing engine and analysis code for a keyword-based
  mapping study of ten Maryland state and local government
  cybersecurity policy documents against 22 controls drawn from 13
  NIST SP 800-53 Rev 5 families. The study reports a mean coverage
  of 49.1 percent and systemic gaps in account management,
  encryption at rest, access control policy and incident reporting.
  The repository also contains the ProofLayer system itself,
  including an LLM gap-analysis stage and a cost-aware model
  routing layer, both of which are described but not evaluated in
  the paper.
keywords:
  - cybersecurity compliance auditing
  - government policy analysis
  - NIST SP 800-53
  - large language models
  - control gap analysis
license: MIT
